# Project Context

The application is structured into two distinct environments:

- Administration Environment
- Workspace Environment

The goal is to maintain completely separated flows for model operations
across these environments.

Model operations must respect environment boundaries at all times.

---

## 1. Administration Environment (Admin Space)

This environment is used by users with administrative roles, including:

- superadmin
- admin

Rules:

- Administrative operations must be isolated from workspace operations
- Admin logic must not be mixed with customer logic
- Admin controllers must not handle workspace-specific behavior

---

## 2. Workspace Environment (Workspace)

This environment is used by users with the role:

- customer

Rules:

- All customer-facing operations must be handled within the Workspace environment
- Business flows for customers must remain separate from administrative flows
- Workspace logic must not depend on admin-specific controllers
- Questi utenti possono avere delle relazioni con i buildings, e per ogni relazione viene espresso un ruolo tra:
    - admin
    - member

There is a dedicated controller:

- `WorkspaceController`

The `WorkspaceController` is responsible for handling all operations
performed by customer users within the workspace environment.

### 2.1 Building Membership Rules

Users may have relationships with buildings.

This relationship represents a membership and must always include a role.

#### 2.1.1 Allowed Roles

The role must be one of the following:

- `admin`
- `member`

#### 2.1.2 Rules

- The relationship between users and buildings must explicitly define the user's role
- The role must always be present and must never be null
- The role must be stored as a controlled value and must not allow arbitrary strings
- Only the allowed roles (`admin`, `member`) are permitted
- Authorization logic must rely on this role to determine permissions within the building context

#### 2.1.3 Responsibility

- A `building admin` has elevated permissions within the building
- A `building member` has standard permissions within the building
